        12:Td80,<h1>Import Rules and Regulations</h1><p>Thinking about importing a car from Japan to Ireland? This page covers which cars can be imported, how they are shipped, the duty and VAT charged when the car arrives, and the Vehicle Registration Tax paid when it is registered.</p><h2>Which Cars Can Be Imported</h2><h3>Vehicle Age</h3><p>Ireland sets <strong>no age limit</strong> on imported cars. Age matters only for tax: a car more than 30 years old pays a flat Vehicle Registration Tax.</p><h3>Steering Position</h3><p>Both <strong>right-hand drive and left-hand drive</strong> cars can be imported. Most Japanese cars are right-hand drive, the same as cars sold in Ireland.</p><h3>Vehicle Type</h3><p><strong>Passenger cars</strong> with up to 9 seats, including the driver's seat.</p><h2>Inspections</h2><ul><li><strong>In Japan:</strong> none. Ireland does not ask for an inspection certificate before the car ships.</li><li><strong>In Ireland:</strong> the car is inspected by the National Car Testing Service (NCTS) within seven days of arriving. The NCTS registers the car and works out its Vehicle Registration Tax at that appointment.</li></ul><h2>Shipping</h2><ul><li><strong>Arrival ports:</strong> Dublin or Cork</li><li><strong>Shipping method:</strong> RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off)</li><li><strong>Shipping line:</strong> Höegh Autoliners, sailing monthly</li><li><strong>Time at sea:</strong> 28-45 days</li></ul><h2>Duties and Taxes</h2><p>Customs duty and VAT are worked out on the <strong>CIF value</strong>: the price of the car plus the sea freight to Ireland.</p><ul><li><strong>Customs duty:</strong> 0% for cars made in Japan, and 10% of the CIF value for cars made elsewhere. The 0% rate comes from the EU–Japan trade agreement.</li><li><strong>Import VAT:</strong> 23% of the CIF value plus customs duty.</li></ul><h2>Vehicle Registration Tax (VRT)</h2><ul><li><strong>VRT:</strong> a percentage of the car's Open Market Selling Price, set by its CO2 emissions: from 7% (at least €140) in the lowest band to 41% (at least €820) in the highest, across twenty bands.</li><li><strong>NOx charge:</strong> €5 for each mg/km of NOx up to 40, €15 for each mg/km from 40 to 80, and €25 above that, capped at €4,850 for diesel cars and €600 for other cars.</li><li><strong>Electric cars:</strong> no NOx charge, and up to €5,000 off VRT until 31 December 2026. The reduction shrinks for cars valued above €40,000 and ends at €50,000.</li><li><strong>Cars more than 30 years old:</strong> a flat €200 VRT and no NOx charge.</li></ul><p>Where Revenue has not yet valued a car, the VRT shown on this site is an estimate. The final amount is set when the car is registered.</p><h2>After Registration</h2><ul><li><strong>NCT test:</strong> €60, for cars first registered four or more years ago.</li><li><strong>Tyre charge:</strong> €14.</li><li><strong>Motor tax:</strong> paid yearly, set by CO2 emissions for cars first registered from July 2008 and by engine size before that. Cars more than 30 years old pay €56.</li></ul><h2>Step by Step</h2><ol><li>The car is booked onto a RoRo sailing and the export documents are issued in Japan.</li><li>The car arrives, the customs declaration is filed, and duty and VAT are paid. Filing needs an EORI number.</li><li>The NCTS inspects the car within seven days of arrival and works out its VRT.</li><li>The car goes onto the Irish register and its plates are issued.</li></ol>13:T2185,<h1>Privacy Policy – Carbarn Ireland</h1><h2>1. Introduction</h2><p>This Privacy Policy ("Policy") explains how <strong>Carbarn LLC, Japan</strong> ("Carbarn", "we", "us" or "our") collects, uses and protects your personal information when you use this website or our services to import vehicles from Japan to Ireland.</p><p>Carbarn operates from Japan. By using this website or placing an order, you agree to the practices described in this Policy. Where we determine why and how your personal data is processed, we act as the data controller for that processing.</p><h2>2. What Information We Collect</h2><p>2.1 Personal information — to process your vehicle order and provide export services, we may collect:</p><ul><li>Full name</li><li>Contact details (email address, telephone number, delivery address)</li><li>Identity documentation where export or customs documentation requires it</li><li>Purchase history and vehicle preferences</li><li>Browsing behaviour on our platform</li><li>Payment confirmation, received through secure third-party processing</li></ul><p>2.2 Financial information — we accept bank transfer and credit or debit card. Card details are handled by the payment processor and are not stored by Carbarn.</p><h2>3. Why We Process Your Information and On What Basis</h2><p>Your personal data is used to:</p><ul><li>Perform the contract for your purchase, shipment and export documentation</li><li>Meet legal obligations under Japanese export law and to support customs formalities at destination</li><li>Operate and improve this website, on the basis of our legitimate interests</li><li>Send optional service notices or promotional updates, where you have consented</li></ul><p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with third parties other than as described in this Policy.</p><h2>4. Who We Share Your Information With</h2><ul><li><strong>Shipping lines and logistics partners</strong> — to arrange export and ocean carriage</li><li><strong>IT and hosting service providers</strong> — to operate this website securely</li><li><strong>Japanese authorities</strong> — to comply with vehicle export regulations</li><li><strong>Customs brokers and clearing agents you appoint</strong> — where you ask us to release documents to them</li><li><strong>Legal and regulatory bodies</strong> — where disclosure is required by law</li><li><strong>Google</strong> — where you have consented, to provide website analytics and advertising measurement (see section 8)</li></ul><h2>5. Retention</h2><p>We keep your personal data for as long as needed to complete your order and to satisfy the export, tax and accounting record-keeping periods that apply to us, after which it is deleted or anonymised.</p><h2>6. International Transfers</h2><p>Carbarn is established in Japan, so personal data collected from customers in Ireland is transferred outside the European Economic Area. Japan has been recognised by the European Commission as providing an adequate level of data protection, and we apply appropriate safeguards to transfers to our service providers where that recognition does not cover them.</p><h2>7. Data Security</h2><p>We apply technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data, including:</p><ul><li>Encryption in transit across the platform</li><li>Restricted internal access to customer records</li><li>Hosting on secured servers</li><li>No storage of full card credentials</li></ul><p>We maintain these standards, though transmission of data over the internet carries inherent risk.</p><h2>8. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2><p>We use cookies and similar technologies on this website. Strictly necessary cookies are always active because the website cannot function without them. All other cookies are optional and are used only if you consent to them, in accordance with the Irish ePrivacy Regulations and the GDPR.</p><p><strong>Strictly necessary cookies.</strong> These enable core functions of the website, such as signing in to your account, remembering your chosen currency and keeping the vehicles you have saved.</p><p><strong>Analytics cookies (“Help us improve”).</strong> With your consent, we use Google Analytics, a web analytics service provided by Google, to understand how visitors use our website, including which vehicles, pages and searches are viewed, so that we can improve the website and the vehicles we offer. We do not send your name, telephone number or email address to Google Analytics.</p><p><strong>Advertising cookies (“Ads for cars you’d like”).</strong> With your consent, Google may use information about your visits to our website to show you advertisements for vehicles that may interest you on Google services and other websites, and to help us measure the effectiveness of our advertising.</p><p><strong>Measurement from our systems.</strong> If you have consented to analytics cookies, we may also send Google Analytics a record of certain actions connected with your visit, such as when an enquiry, order or payment is recorded. These records are linked to the pseudonymous identifier that Google Analytics has assigned to your browser and, if you are signed in, to an internal customer reference. They do not include your name or contact details. If you have not consented, no such records are sent.</p><p><strong>Legal basis and your choices.</strong> Our legal basis for using optional cookies, and for the related measurement, is your consent. When you first visit the website you can accept or reject optional cookies, or choose individual categories, and you can change or withdraw your consent at any time by selecting “Cookie settings” at the bottom of any page. Withdrawing your consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before you withdrew it. We remember your choice for six months, after which we will ask you again. You can also block or delete cookies through your browser settings.</p><p><strong>Retention and international transfers.</strong> Google Analytics data is kept for up to 14 months. Google may process this information in the United States and in other countries outside the European Economic Area. Google states that such transfers are protected by appropriate safeguards, including the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. For more information, please see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from websites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>9. Your Rights</h2><p>Under the EU General Data Protection Regulation and the Irish Data Protection Acts, you have the right to:</p><ul><li>Be informed about how your personal data is processed</li><li>Request access to a copy of the personal data we hold about you</li><li>Have inaccurate personal data corrected</li><li>Request erasure of your personal data, where the law allows it</li><li>Request that processing be restricted, in defined circumstances</li><li>Receive your data in a portable format, or have it transmitted to another controller</li><li>Object to processing carried out on the basis of legitimate interests, and to direct marketing at any time</li><li>Withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing carried out before withdrawal</li></ul><p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at info@carbarn.ie. If you are not satisfied with our response, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the <strong>Data Protection Commission</strong>, Ireland's supervisory authority for data protection.</p><h2>10. External Links</h2><p>This website may link to third-party platforms. Carbarn is not responsible for the privacy practices of those external sites.</p><h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2><p>We do not knowingly collect personal data from individuals under 18. If we become aware that we have, we will delete it.</p><h2>12. Updates to This Policy</h2><p>We may revise this Policy following legal or regulatory change, platform changes, or customer feedback. The version published on this site is the current one.</p><h2>13. Governing Law</h2><p>This Policy is governed by the laws of Japan. This does not affect the data protection rights available to you as a person located in Ireland, or your right to complain to the Data Protection Commission.</p><h2>Contact Us</h2><p>Email: info@carbarn.ie</p><p>Operated by: <strong>Carbarn LLC, Japan</strong></p>14:T1442,<h1>Terms and Conditions – Carbarn Ireland</h1><h2>1. Introduction</h2><p>These Terms and Conditions ("Agreement") govern the relationship between you (the "Purchaser") and <strong>Carbarn LLC</strong> ("Carbarn", "we", "us" or "our"), a Japan-registered company, in connection with the purchase and export of used vehicles from Japan to Ireland.</p><p>By using this website and purchasing a vehicle through us, you agree to these terms. The contract of sale is made between the Purchaser and Carbarn LLC (Japan).</p><h2>2. Nature of Business</h2><ul><li>Carbarn LLC is a Japan-based company engaged in the export of used vehicles, including to Ireland.</li><li>Carbarn owns the vehicles it lists, and vehicle transactions, ownership transfer and export documentation originate from Japan.</li><li>Carbarn's responsibility concludes on handover of the vehicle to the shipping line at the port of export in Japan.</li><li>Carbarn does not act as a customs clearing agent in Ireland and does not carry out registration with the National Car Testing Service on the Purchaser's behalf.</li></ul><h2>3. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2><ul><li>This Agreement is governed by the laws of Japan.</li><li>Where the Purchaser is a consumer resident in Ireland, this choice of law does not remove the protection of mandatory Irish and European Union consumer law, and the Purchaser may bring proceedings in the courts of Ireland.</li></ul><h2>4. Vehicle Condition and Inspection</h2><ul><li>Ireland requires no Japan-side pre-shipment inspection, so no inspection certificate from a Japanese inspection body is issued for this route.</li><li>Every listing carries photographs, the Carbarn inspection comments, the full inspection report and the auction grade.</li><li>Vehicles are used and are sold in the condition described in the inspection report and auction sheet.</li><li>Recorded odometer readings are taken from the auction sheet and export documentation and are reported as recorded.</li></ul><h2>5. Shipping and Delivery</h2><ul><li>Vehicles are shipped by RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off) from Japan.</li><li>Destination ports are Dublin and Cork.</li><li>Ocean transit is 28–45 days, on a monthly sailing schedule operated by Höegh Autoliners, and depends on vessel scheduling.</li><li>Once the vehicle is handed to the shipping line, Carbarn does not control vessel delays, port charges or terminal handling.</li></ul><h2>6. Payment Terms</h2><ul><li>We accept bank transfer and credit or debit card.</li><li>Payment details are issued only on an official Carbarn proforma invoice after the quote is confirmed.</li><li>Bank charges, intermediary fees and exchange costs are the responsibility of the Purchaser.</li><li>Shipment arrangements begin once the payment terms stated on the proforma invoice have been met.</li></ul><h2>7. Customs Clearance and Registration in Ireland</h2><ul><li>The Purchaser is responsible for customs clearance, duty, VAT, Vehicle Registration Tax and registration in Ireland, and for the costs of each.</li><li>Duty and tax are assessed by Revenue. Registration is completed through the National Car Testing Service, which registers imported vehicles on behalf of Revenue.</li><li>The vehicle must be presented for its NCTS inspection within seven days of arriving in the State.</li><li>The Purchaser is responsible for holding the customs registrations needed to lodge an import declaration in Ireland.</li></ul><p>Documents supplied by Carbarn:</p><ul><li>Registration Certificate (Country of Origin)</li><li>Export Certificate</li><li>Original Invoice</li><li>Bill of Lading</li><li>Condition Report</li></ul><h2>8. Cancellation and Consumer Rights</h2><ul><li>Where the Purchaser is a consumer contracting at a distance, the cancellation rights conferred by Irish consumer law apply and are not restricted by this Agreement.</li><li>Outside those statutory rights, an order may be cancelled before the vehicle is handed to the shipping line, subject to costs already incurred.</li><li>Once the vehicle has been handed to the shipping line, cancellation is subject to the statutory position and to the costs of shipment and return.</li></ul><h2>9. Disclaimer and Limitation of Liability</h2><ul><li>Carbarn is not liable for port delays, demurrage, terminal handling charges, or delays in customs clearance or registration in Ireland.</li><li>Carbarn is not liable for loss or damage occurring after the vehicle is handed to the shipping line, which is covered by the carriage and insurance arrangements in place.</li><li>Nothing in this Agreement limits liability that cannot be limited by law, including liability to consumers under mandatory Irish and European Union consumer law.</li></ul><h2>10. Data Protection</h2><ul><li>We collect only the customer data needed for order processing and export compliance.</li><li>Customer information is not sold, and is shared only as set out in our Privacy Policy.</li><li>Full details, including your rights and the complaint route to the Data Protection Commission, are in our Privacy Policy.</li></ul><h2>11. Contact</h2><p>Email: info@carbarn.ie</p><p>Operated by: <strong>Carbarn LLC, Japan</strong></p>2:["$","html",null,{"lang":"en-IE","className":"__variable_369f12","suppressHydrationWarning":true,"style":"$undefined","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"id":"ga-gtag-init","strategy":"afterInteractive","children":"$10"}],["$","body",null,{"suppressHydrationWarning":true,"className":"font-[family-name:var(--font-manrope)] font-normal antialiased bg-white","children":["$","$L11",null,{"config":{"id":28,"code":"IE","name":"Ireland","flag":"🇮🇪","website":"www.carbarn.ie","inspection":null,"inspectionFee":null,"inspectionFeeCurrency":null,"dutySource":"RULE_SET","maxAge":{"cars":9999,"vans":9999,"trucks":9999},"minAge":{},"ageBasis":null,"arrivalPorts":["Dublin","Cork"],"shipping":"RORO","currency":"EUR","countryOfOrigin":"Japan","approxArrivalTimeInDays":"28-45","excludedBrands":[],"heroImageUrl":null,"mapImageUrl":null,"heroTitle":"Drive Japanese <span class=\"font-bold\">Used Cars in Ireland</span> with Clear Costs Upfront","googleSiteVerificationId":null,"gaMeasurementId":"G-0YKBCVHBNX","ga4ApiSecretSet":true,"canonicalHost":"www.carbarn.ie","languageRegion":"en-IE","logoUrl":"https://fastlycb.s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com/country-config/carbarn-ir-logo.png","facebookPageId":null,"officeAddress":null,"officeHours":null,"officeMapEmbedUrl":null,"localEntityName":null,"customsAuthorityNote":"Buyers are responsible for paying all duties and taxes due to Revenue (the Office of the Revenue Commissioners) and for registering the vehicle through the National Car Testing Service (NCTS), which registers imported vehicles on Revenue's behalf.","shippingRouteDescription":"Your vehicle will be shipped from Japan to Dublin or Cork Port via RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off) shipping. Once it arrives, you can clear it through your preferred clearing agent and collect it from the port, then have it inspected by the NCTS (National Car Testing Service) within seven days of arriving.","aboutContent":null,"socialMediaLinks":{"facebook":"https://www.facebook.com/carbarn.ie/","instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/carbarn.ie/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/@CarbarnIE"},"dutyPercentages":[{"name":"Import Duty","percentage":10},{"name":"VAT","percentage":23}],"faqs":[{"question":"Are there any hidden costs?","answer":"The listed price covers the vehicle and ocean freight from Japan. Customs duty, VAT and Vehicle Registration Tax (VRT) are paid in Ireland and are quoted separately."},{"question":"Does the EU–Japan trade agreement mean I pay no customs duty?","answer":"We quote the standard 10% customs duty. A lower rate can apply where documents proving the car's Japanese origin are available for that particular car, which is rare for cars bought at auction."},{"question":"How are customs duty and VAT worked out in Ireland?","answer":"Customs duty is 10% of the CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) value — the price of the car plus shipping. VAT is 23% of that value plus the duty."},{"question":"How are vehicles shipped from Japan to Ireland?","answer":"By RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off) ship from Japan to Dublin or Cork, sailing once a month with Höegh Autoliners."},{"question":"How do I check the vehicle condition?","answer":"Every listing carries photographs, the Carbarn inspection comments, the full inspection report, and the auction grade, so the condition can be verified before you commit."},{"question":"How long does it take for the vehicle to arrive in Ireland?","answer":"Shipping from Japan to Dublin or Cork takes 28-45 days, depending on the sailing and the ship's schedule."},{"question":"What is VRT and how is the estimate worked out?","answer":"Vehicle Registration Tax (VRT) is paid when you register the car in Ireland: 7% to 41% of the Open Market Selling Price, based on carbon-dioxide (CO₂) emissions, plus a NOx charge. We use each car's official Japanese CO₂ and NOx figures and Revenue's own valuation where Revenue lists the model; otherwise the VRT is marked indicative, and Revenue confirms the final amount at registration."},{"question":"What is the age restriction on imported cars in Ireland?","answer":"You can import a car or van of any age into Ireland. There is no upper age limit and no minimum age. Vehicle Registration Tax is based on the car's carbon-dioxide (CO₂) emissions, not on its age."},{"question":"What payment methods do you accept?","answer":"Carbarn accepts Bank Transfer and Credit / Debit Card. Payment details are issued only on an official Carbarn proforma invoice after your quote is confirmed."},{"question":"Which port will my vehicle arrive at?","answer":"Your vehicle arrives at Dublin or Cork. Höegh Autoliners sails the route once a month, carrying vehicles by RoRo (Roll-on/Roll-off)."}],"shippingSchedules":[],"heroDescription":"Carbarn ships Japanese cars to Ireland from its own stock and from the live Japan auctions, giving Irish buyers inspected cars, clear costs before you order, and monthly sailings.","importRules":"$12","privecyAndPolicy":"$13","termsAnsConditions":"$14","status":"ACTIVE","shippingIncluded":true,"supportEmail":"info@carbarn.ie","supportPhone":null,"supportWhatsapp":null,"freightRatePerCbmUsd":125,"priceRoundingStep":100,"shippingFrequency":"Monthly","shippingCarrier":"Höegh Autoliners","stockLandedCostEnabled":true,"stockSource":"JP_STOCK","primaryListing":"AUCTION","auctionSettings":{"tier":"BID","depositMode":"STRIPE","landedCost":"DUTY_ENGINE","allowedCategories":["PASSENGER"],"steering":["RHD"],"ban":null,"agentFee":null,"popularCategories":["hybrid","small-petrol","suv","family-7-seaters","sports"],"depositRule":{"bands":[{"uptoJpy":1500000,"amountJpy":150000,"percent":null},{"uptoJpy":3000000,"amountJpy":300000,"percent":null},{"uptoJpy":5000000,"amountJpy":500000,"percent":null},{"uptoJpy":8000000,"amountJpy":null,"percent":15},{"uptoJpy":null,"amountJpy":null,"percent":20}],"roundUpTo":500}},"features":{"carSpecsEnabled":false,"carSpecsClosedAs":"GONE","seoTemplatesEnabled":true,"legalComplianceBadge":false,"payAtOfficeEnabled":false,"cardPaymentsEnabled":true,"taxFactsEnabled":true,"localCurrencyFirst":true,"combinedProductLayout":false,"proseLayer":true,"homepageComposition":false,"homepageSections":[],"heroFacts":[],"requireDutyToList":false,"searchIndexing":true,"searchPages":{"home":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"auctionHome":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"auctionCategories":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":"CHOSEN","chosen":["hybrid","small-petrol","suv"],"withoutStock":null},"auctionMakes":{"index":false,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"auctionModels":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":"CHOSEN","chosen":["toyota/yaris","suzuki/jimny","toyota/land-cruiser","toyota/hilux","nissan/juke","suzuki/swift","toyota/prius","honda/fit","subaru/impreza","nissan/note","toyota/aqua","toyota/hiace","mazda/cx5","nissan/xtrail","toyota/c-hr"],"withoutStock":null},"auctionModelCodes":{"index":false,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"auctionLots":{"index":false,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"stockHome":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"stockModels":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":false},"stockCars":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"importRules":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"howToBuy":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"faq":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"dutyCalculator":{"index":false,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"shippingSchedule":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"about":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"contact":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"blog":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"blogPosts":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"specs":{"index":false,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"privacy":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null},"terms":{"index":true,"follow":true,"mode":null,"chosen":null,"withoutStock":null}},"cookieConsent":true},"paymentMethods":[{"label":"Bank Transfer","note":null},{"label":"Credit / Debit Card","note":null}],"cardPayments":true,"bankDetails":null,"requiredDocuments":["Registration Certificate (Country of Origin)","Export Certificate","Original Invoice","Bill of Lading","Condition Report"],"featuredShelf":null},"region":"IE","children":["$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b"]}]}